# Manifold level 7
# What a body can do (stage 4b), growing with the stage: aim and throw on the open floor, near or far
# by how long the throw is held, at a target 15 m away; crouch (or roll) under a low passage that
# standing does not fit; and walk towards a lamp an eye watches: standing, it sees you soon; crouched
# (lower, and half as easy to see), only much closer.
title What a body can do
spawn -5 1 6
facing 0 0 -1
ambient 0.15

box 0 -0.5 0  10 0.5 10  grid  name floor

# The low passage, 4 m long and 2.4 m wide: two walls and a slab whose bottom is 1.15 m up. Standing
# (1.6 m) it does not fit; crouched (1.1 m), it passes.
box -1.6 0.95 -2  0.4 0.95 2    color #6f6a62
box 1.6 0.95 -2   0.4 0.95 2    color #6f6a62
box 0 1.4 -2      1.2 0.25 2    color #5a4a38  name low

# The lamp and the eye (beside the post, so the post does not hide you): walking from the far end (z = 9)
# towards the lamp, standing, the eye sees you
# about 5 m from it; crouched, under 2 m.
box 5 1.4 0       0.06 1.4 0.06 color #4a4440
lamp 5 3 0        7 1           name lamp
watcher 7 2 -9    16 70 0.35    rotate y 180  name eye

# The target (the throw's charge): a board 15 m ahead of the start, a plate in front of it, and a lamp
# above it that lights for good once a ball reaches the plate. A tap (F) throws short of it; held a
# second, and aimed a little up, the ball gets there.
box -5 1.5 -9.6     1 1.5 0.1     color #5a4a38  name board
sensor plate  -5 1.6 -9.2   1 1 0.3  name target
lamp -5 3.4 -9.2    4 1           signal struck  name target_lamp
signal hit      zone target
signal never
signal struck   latch hit never

# A training dummy (stage 4c), at the side of the start, looking into the room: thrown at, it is hurt
# (twice on the head), goes down when its points run out, and is back on its feet three seconds later.
sensor dummy  -8 1 2   0.3 0.8 0.3  rotate y -90  name dummy_spot

# Weapons to pick up (stage 4c), behind the start: walk into one to carry it, and X (or a click while
# the aim camera holds the mouse) uses it. A dart (hitscan), a bolt (a projectile), a stick (a strike).
sensor weapon  -6.5 0.5 8.2   0.4 0.5 0.4  kind 1  name dart_rack
sensor weapon  -5 0.5 8.6     0.4 0.5 0.4  kind 2  name bolt_rack
sensor weapon  -3.5 0.5 8.2   0.4 0.5 0.4  kind 3  name stick_rack

# A pane 2 cm thin, before a second dummy (stage 4c): a bolt at 80 m/s goes 1.3 m a step, and still
# never crosses it.
box -8 1 -3   1 1 0.01  color #8ab0c0  name pane
sensor dummy  -8 1 -5   0.3 0.8 0.3  name dummy_behind
